{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789661308,"nonce":"fwhfURzvXdKdIa4OAxUWz0vg3d4=","title":"Spike: demonstrate lost ops with two concurrent writers","message":"`repository/gogit.go` UpdateRef is a plain SetReference (no compare-and-swap) and `dag.Entity.Commit` does not re-read before writing. Prediction: two processes each appending an op to the same issue -\u003e last ref write wins, the other's commit dangles silently.\n\nWrite a test (two RepoCache-less writers on one repo, or two goroutines with two `GoGitRepo` handles) that reproduces this. It becomes the regression test for the write-lock work. Both packages involved are pristine; the fix lives above them.","files":null}]}